declaration scope MemberOfHousehold:
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input world content W.World
  input dependant content W.Entity
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  ## True when the caller *enumerated* the taxpayer rather than being given one.
  ## SARA reaches the spouse parenthetical with `Taxp` still unbound, and the
  ## guard then binds it from the marriage's own agents, so the exclusion fires
  ## on any qualifying marriage naming the dependant -- including one where the
  ## dependant is the only agent, and so is read as married to themselves. The
  ## `Dependent \== Taxp` test above it was already spent, having run while
  ## `Taxp` was a fresh variable. (H) therefore contributes nothing at all in
  ## that mode, and a port that lets it contribute finds dependants SARA does
  ## not. See D24.
  input taxpayer_generated content boolean
  ## The mirror image, and the mode §2(b)(3)(B) runs in: SARA reaches (H) with
  ## `Dependent` still unbound, having spent `Dependent \== Taxp` on a fresh
  ## variable, and the spouse guard's `agent_(Marriage,Dependent)` then binds
  ## the dependant from the marriage's own agents. The exclusion therefore
  ## fires on *any* qualifying marriage naming the taxpayer -- the taxpayer is
  ## an agent of it, so the dependant conjunct is free -- and (H) is false for
  ## every candidate. A port that tests the marriage against each candidate in
  ## turn finds dependants SARA does not. See D50.
  input dependant_generated content boolean
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## The parenthetical: a spouse during the taxable year is excluded.
  output spouse_excluded content boolean
  ## `s152_d_2_H/6` granted by the case, windows and all.
  output injected content list of K.Window
  output windows content list of K.Window
  output holds content boolean
